# The Piper PA-28-180 Cherokee's checklists: this project's own, in its own words.
#
# **They are not taken from the aeroplane's flight manual.** No such
# manual was read to write them. What they follow is the ordinary
# practice for the type, in the order it is flown; the speeds and
# settings in them are this project's own figures, assets/figures/pa28.xml,
# whose sources docs/ASSETS.md records, and the flight model itself
# wherever the model is what decides - a lever's gate, a flap's travel,
# an engine's idle.
#
#   phase NAME                       one of: before-start, taxi, take-off,
#                                    climb, cruise, descent, approach,
#                                    landing, after-landing
#   check PROPERTY OP VALUE TEXT...  an item the aircraft can see done
#   range PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT...  the same, where a band shows it done
#   confirm TEXT...                  an item only the pilot can see done
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/checklist.hpp owns the format.
#
# The Cherokee's undercarriage is fixed and its propeller fixed-pitch, so
# nothing here names the gear or a pitch lever. Its fuel selector has no both
# position, and neither its electric fuel pump nor its carburettor heat is in
# the flight model: those are the pilot's to confirm.

phase before-start
confirm Walk-round done, tanks dipped, and the propeller area called clear
confirm The one door latched, seats upright and harnesses fastened
confirm Fuel selector on the fuller tank, for the Cherokee has no both
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle open a quarter of an inch
confirm Master switch on, and the electric fuel pump on for the start

phase taxi
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 500 Engine running and idling evenly
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up, the lever down between the seats
confirm Brakes tried as the aeroplane first moves
confirm Compass and the turn coordinator watched round the turns
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.4 Taxi at a walking pace on low power

phase take-off
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 25.5 Flaps up, or twenty-five degrees off a short field
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
range fcs/pitch-trim-cmd-norm -0.35 0.35 Stabilator trim set for take-off
confirm Electric fuel pump on, controls free, and the magnetos dropped evenly at 2,000 rpm
check propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm >= 2275.0 Full throttle, and 2,275 rpm or better standing still
check velocities/vc-kts >= 48.0 Ease the wheel back at 48 knots and let her fly off

phase climb
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Throttle wide open
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up once the aeroplane is climbing away
range velocities/vc-kts 70.0 88.0 Climb at 74 to 85 knots
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich below 5,000 feet
confirm Electric fuel pump off, and the oil temperature and pressure in the green

phase cruise
range propulsion/engine[0]/engine-rpm 2250.0 2700.0 Cruising rpm set between 2,300 and 2,650
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm <= 0.95 Mixture leaned for the cruising height
confirm Tanks changed on the half hour, and the altimeter set
confirm The aeroplane trimmed to hold its height hands off

phase descent
range fcs/throttle-cmd-norm 0.10 0.65 Power back for the descent
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.85 Mixture enriched as the aeroplane comes down
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up until the speed is back in the white arc
confirm Altimeter set to the field's pressure, and its weather noted
confirm Carburettor heat as the air asks, and the cabin heat as wanted

phase approach
check fcs/mixture-cmd-norm >= 0.95 Mixture full rich
confirm Electric fuel pump on, and the fuel on the fuller tank
range velocities/vc-kts 64.0 80.0 Approach at 68 to 75 knots
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 0.0 40.5 Flaps as the approach asks, up to the full forty degrees
confirm Landing light on, the runway in sight and the circuit clear

phase landing
range fcs/flap-pos-deg 25.0 40.5 Flaps twenty-five degrees to full
range velocities/vc-kts 58.0 72.0 Over the fence at 62 to 70 knots
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.25 Throttle closed in the flare
confirm Hold her off and touch down on the main wheels first
confirm Wheel held back as the speed falls, and the brakes used gently

phase after-landing
check fcs/flap-pos-deg <= 0.5 Flaps up
check fcs/throttle-cmd-norm <= 0.35 Throttle back to a taxi power
check velocities/vc-kts <= 30.0 Clear of the runway and slowed to a taxi
confirm Electric fuel pump off, carburettor heat cold
confirm Landing light off, strobes off, and the trim reset
